x86_64-linux  cxx1 emits a cleanup region for every scope holding an object with a destructor, and clang omits one when nothing in the region can throw - nothing here can: the loop has no call, and a destructor is noexcept in C++11. So clang references no personality routine and no _Unwind_Resume, and cxx1 references both. A difference in pruning, not in what runs; pruning a region is a rule about the calls inside it and belongs with the noexcept work, not with jumps
arm64-darwin  cxx1 emits a cleanup region for every scope holding an object with a destructor, and clang omits one when nothing in the region can throw - nothing here can: the loop has no call, and a destructor is noexcept in C++11. So clang references no personality routine and no _Unwind_Resume, and cxx1 references both. A difference in pruning, not in what runs; pruning a region is a rule about the calls inside it and belongs with the noexcept work, not with jumps
